<header><p class="enc-kicker">Place · island</p><h1 class="enc-title">Madagascar</h1></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Madagascar is the world's fourth-largest island, in the <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/indian-ocean">Indian Ocean</a> off south-eastern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/africa">Africa</a>. Settled by Austronesian seafarers from South-<a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-asia">East Asia</a> and by people from <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/east-africa">East Africa</a> during the first millennium CE, it developed many kingdoms, of which the Merina unified most of the island in the 19th century. <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/france">France</a> conquered it in 1895–1896, and it became independent in 1960; its wildlife, such as the lemurs, is found nowhere else.</p><figure class="enc-fig"><img src="/images/encyclopedia/madagascar.jpg" alt="Madagascar" width="320" height="320" fetchpriority="high"><figcaption>Image: M.Bitton · CC BY-SA 4.0 · <a href="https://commons.wikimedia.org/wiki/File:Madagascar_(centered_orthographic_projection).svg" target="_blank" rel="noopener">Wikimedia Commons</a></figcaption></figure></div>
